            <ArticleTitle>Ischaemic heart disease, and vehicle travel.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>401-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mathematical data are presented supporting a relationship between road accident deaths (RAD), male and female, and ischaemic heart disease (IHD) deaths, male and female, in Australia. It is suggested that RAD on a national scale are a function of vehicle usage, for both males and females, and in turn, vehicle usage creates stress on bodily function resulting in IHD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
